module tasks.`2026-11-25-term-oracle-handoff`

task TermOracleHandoff {
  title "Term Oracle: take the 2026-11-25 handoff, green main, land and close the six open tasks"
  verify $ git -C /Users/feral/mydev/bboxy450-term fetch -q origin && git -C /Users/feral/mydev/bboxy450-term log -1 --format=%G? origin/main | grep -qx G
  paths ".bboxy/**"
  brief """
    # Term Oracle handoff, 2026-11-25

    ROLE: ORACLE, for the term swarm. Delegated by the sudo seat on the operator's order "close tasks!".

    Brief: ~/mydev/bboxy450-term-oracle-handoff.md (copy /tmp/bboxy-oracle-handoff.md). Its operator orders and lessons apply.

    Steps:
    1. make tool-usage DAYS=1; record the number in the handoff.
    2. One full make test on origin/main (7d722969a or later) in a fresh worktree. It must be fully green.
    3. Delegate the open tasks to Codex executors, at most 2 compiling at once: artifact-claim-recovery-race and build-dirs-never-index first, then kb-watch-rescan-fallback and workspace-index-bounds, then harness-test-debt and dream-q3b-read-prepare.
    4. Verify each landing from the diff and logs. task_accept, task_close, seat_close the executor, workspace_release.
    5. Report: task_report with a report record, the full make test exit and its log path, and the final state of all six tasks.

    Already done by sudo: the outgoing Oracle seat 01M8764DX3P3XKP4DF8R2DANYR is closed.
    """

  managed {
    assignee = json"\"seat:01M89ZRSC32VXKQKRMXZ87PFCT\""
    authorship = json"{\"kind\":\"seat\",\"process_generation\":\"1\",\"public_key\":\"XLMAqZTUlsEIvVxlAso8YDW5Ud3ShPEW3Kz+hD0wm1c=\",\"signer\":\"seat:01M89Z74HN4GSHEPS6TC0H6FDX\"}"
